# Delegate implementation patterns — Kora 2.x

Patterns for implementing a generated `*ApiDelegate`. Java and Kotlin are kept behaviourally
aligned; the Kotlin variants follow the named-argument rule for generated models.
Placeholders are `${...}`.

Kora 2.0 contracts are **synchronous**: no `Mono`, `Flux`, `CompletionStage` or `suspend`
delegate exists, and `Context` has been removed from the framework.

---

## 1. Skeleton

```java
package ${basePackage}.delegate;

import io.koraframework.common.annotation.Component;
import ${basePackage}.api.${Api}ApiDelegate;
import ${basePackage}.api.${Api}ApiResponses;
import ${basePackage}.model.*;

@Component                                   // io.koraframework.common.annotation.Component
public final class ${Api}Delegate implements ${Api}ApiDelegate {

    private final ${Service} ${service};

    public ${Api}Delegate(${Service} ${service}) {
        this.${service} = ${service};
    }
}
```

```kotlin
package ${basePackage}.delegate

import io.koraframework.common.annotation.Component
import ${basePackage}.api.${Api}ApiDelegate
import ${basePackage}.api.${Api}ApiResponses

@Component
class ${Api}Delegate(private val ${service}: ${Service}) : ${Api}ApiDelegate
```

The generated method declares `throws Exception` in Java; an override may narrow it away.
Kotlin overrides are plain `fun`.

---

## 2. Lookup with 200 / 404

```java
@Override
public ${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse get${Entity}ById(long id) {
    var found = ${service}.find(id);
    return found == null
            ? new ${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse.Get${Entity}ById404ApiResponse()
            : new ${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse.Get${Entity}ById200ApiResponse(found);
}
```

```kotlin
override fun get${Entity}ById(id: Long): ${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse {
    val found = ${service}.find(id)
        ?: return ${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse.Get${Entity}ById404ApiResponse()
    return ${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse.Get${Entity}ById200ApiResponse(found)
}
```

When Java infers the record type instead of the sealed supertype (typically in a ternary or a
lambda), name the target type explicitly:

```java
return ${service}.find(id)
        .<${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse>map(e ->
                new ${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse.Get${Entity}ById200ApiResponse(e))
        .orElseGet(() ->
                new ${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse.Get${Entity}ById404ApiResponse());
```

---

## 3. Parsing a generated enum — `fromValue`, never `valueOf`

The wire value in the contract (`available`) is not the generated constant (`AVAILABLE`), so
`Enum.valueOf` throws on valid input. This fails only against real data.

```java
@Override
public ${Api}ApiResponses.Find${Entity}ByStatusApiResponse find${Entity}ByStatus(@Nullable String status) {
    final ${Entity}.StatusEnum parsed;
    try {
        parsed = ${Entity}.StatusEnum.fromValue(status);
    } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
        return new ${Api}ApiResponses.Find${Entity}ByStatusApiResponse
                .Find${Entity}ByStatus400ApiResponse(new ErrorResponse("unknown status: " + status));
    }
    return new ${Api}ApiResponses.Find${Entity}ByStatusApiResponse
            .Find${Entity}ByStatus200ApiResponse(${service}.byStatus(parsed));
}
```

```kotlin
override fun find${Entity}ByStatus(status: String?): ${Api}ApiResponses.Find${Entity}ByStatusApiResponse {
    val parsed = try {
        status?.let(${Entity}.StatusEnum::fromValue)
    } catch (_: IllegalArgumentException) {
        null
    } ?: return ${Api}ApiResponses.Find${Entity}ByStatusApiResponse
        .Find${Entity}ByStatus400ApiResponse(ErrorResponse(message = "unknown status: $status"))

    return ${Api}ApiResponses.Find${Entity}ByStatusApiResponse
        .Find${Entity}ByStatus200ApiResponse(${service}.byStatus(parsed))
}
```

Serialise back with `getValue()`.

---

## 4. Building and copying generated models

Java models expose a canonical constructor, a **required-only** constructor (generated whenever
any field is optional) and one `withX` per field:

```java
var created = new ${Entity}(id, name);                       // required-only constructor
var renamed = created.withName(newName).withStatus(status);  // copy helpers
```

Kotlin models keep **spec order** with defaults in place, so an optional property can sit between
two required ones. Always use named arguments:

```kotlin
val created = ${Entity}(id = id, name = name)                // never positional
val renamed = created.copy(name = newName, status = status)
```

A positional Kotlin call compiles only while the argument types happen to line up, and silently
shifts values when the contract changes.

---

## 5. Three-state fields (`JsonNullable`)

A `nullable: true` + not-`required` field is generated as
`io.koraframework.json.common.JsonNullable<T>`, distinguishing absent from explicit null.

```java
@Override
public ${Api}ApiResponses.Patch${Entity}ApiResponse patch${Entity}(long id, ${Entity}Patch patch) {
    var entity = ${service}.find(id);
    if (entity == null) {
        return new ${Api}ApiResponses.Patch${Entity}ApiResponse.Patch${Entity}404ApiResponse();
    }
    if (patch.nickname().isDefined()) {          // key present in the payload
        entity = entity.withNickname(patch.nickname().value());   // value may itself be null
    }
    return new ${Api}ApiResponses.Patch${Entity}ApiResponse
            .Patch${Entity}200ApiResponse(${service}.save(entity));
}
```

```kotlin
override fun patch${Entity}(id: Long, patch: ${Entity}Patch): ${Api}ApiResponses.Patch${Entity}ApiResponse {
    var entity = ${service}.find(id)
        ?: return ${Api}ApiResponses.Patch${Entity}ApiResponse.Patch${Entity}404ApiResponse()
    if (patch.nickname.isDefined) {
        entity = entity.copy(nickname = patch.nickname.value())
    }
    return ${Api}ApiResponses.Patch${Entity}ApiResponse
        .Patch${Entity}200ApiResponse(${service}.save(entity))
}
```

Construct one with `JsonNullable.of(v)`, `JsonNullable.ofNullable(v)`, `JsonNullable.nullValue()`
or `JsonNullable.undefined()`.

---

## 6. Discriminated request bodies

The generated base is a `sealed interface`, so the match is exhaustive without a default branch.

```java
@Override
public ${Api}ApiResponses.SetDeliveryApiResponse setDelivery(long id, Delivery delivery) {
    switch (delivery) {
        case DeliveryCourier c -> ${service}.scheduleCourier(id, c.address());
        case DeliveryPickup p  -> ${service}.schedulePickup(id, p.pointId());
    }
    return new ${Api}ApiResponses.SetDeliveryApiResponse.SetDelivery204ApiResponse();
}
```

```kotlin
override fun setDelivery(id: Long, delivery: Delivery): ${Api}ApiResponses.SetDeliveryApiResponse {
    when (delivery) {
        is DeliveryCourier -> ${service}.scheduleCourier(id, delivery.address)
        is DeliveryPickup  -> ${service}.schedulePickup(id, delivery.pointId)
    }
    return ${Api}ApiResponses.SetDeliveryApiResponse.SetDelivery204ApiResponse()
}
```

