## 7. Reading the authenticated principal

The generated `ApiSecurity` interceptor binds the principal to a JDK `ScopedValue`; read it with
`Principal.current()`. There is no `Context` in Kora 2.0.

```java
var principal = io.koraframework.common.Principal.current();   // @Nullable
if (principal instanceof UserPrincipal user) {
    ${service}.actAs(user.name());
}
```

```kotlin
val user = Principal.current() as? UserPrincipal
```

---

## 8. Raw `HttpServerRequest` access

Only with `configOptions.requestInDelegateParams: "true"`, which prepends `_serverRequest` to
**every** controller and delegate method.

```java
@Override
public ${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse get${Entity}ById(
        HttpServerRequest _serverRequest, long id) {
    var traceId = _serverRequest.headers().getFirst("x-trace-id");
    …
}
```

```kotlin
override fun get${Entity}ById(
    _serverRequest: HttpServerRequest,
    id: Long,
): ${Api}ApiResponses.Get${Entity}ByIdApiResponse {
    val traceId = _serverRequest.headers().getFirst("x-trace-id")
    …
}
```

`HttpServerRequest` is `io.koraframework.http.server.common.request.HttpServerRequest`.

---

## 9. Form and multipart operations

Form fields arrive as a record nested in the **controller**, wired through a generated mapper.
Copy the parameter, including its `@Mapping`, from the generated delegate.

```java
@Override
public ${Api}ApiResponses.UploadApiResponse upload(${Api}ApiController.UploadFormParam form) {
    var part = form.photo();                     // FormMultipart.FormPart for `format: binary`
    ${service}.store(form.name(), part.content());
    return new ${Api}ApiResponses.UploadApiResponse.Upload204ApiResponse();
}
```

Array form fields arrive as lists (an absent optional array is `null`); boolean form values accept
only `true` / `false`.

---

## 10. Errors the contract does not model

Prefer a declared status record. When the contract genuinely has no room for the case, throw:

```java
throw io.koraframework.http.server.common.response.HttpServerResponseException.of(409, "conflict");
```

```kotlin
throw HttpServerResponseException.of(409, "conflict")
```

Constraint violations are already handled: `@Validate` throws `ViolationException` and
`ValidationHttpServerInterceptor` maps it (default `400`).

---

## 11. Anti-patterns

| Do not | Do |
|---|---|
| Hand-write an `@HttpController` for a generated operation | Implement the delegate |
| Edit anything in `build/generated` | `./gradlew clean build --no-build-cache` |
| `Enum.valueOf(raw)` / a hand-written `statusOf` | `MyEnum.fromValue(raw)` |
| Positional construction of a Kotlin model | Named arguments |
| `override suspend fun` / `Mono` / `CompletionStage` | Plain synchronous signatures |
| `@Tag(ApiSecurity.SecurityRequirementTag1.class)` | `@Tag(ApiSecurity.<SchemeName>.class)` |
| Return a raw DTO | Return the generated response record |
| Business logic in the delegate | Inject a service; the delegate only maps |
